# server

The local test server for this project.

**You provide the Paper jar.** Download Paper ${paper_version} yourself from https://papermc.io/downloads/paper and put the jar in this folder. mcflow checks that it really is a Paper jar, but it never downloads one for you.

`mcflow server setup` configures it for local development only: localhost only, offline mode, RCON, the resource pack served from your machine, and ViaVersion (plus ViaBackwards when the test bots need it). Claude drives it through mcflow-server: start, stop, logs, deploys, bots and the quality gates.

Everything else in this folder (worlds, logs, plugins, screenshots) is git-ignored.
